# Project Harness Rules

Read [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) first — it is the table of contents, not an encyclopedia.

## Before claiming work done

Run verification:
- Windows: `.\scripts\verify.ps1`
- macOS/Linux: `./scripts/verify.sh`

## When tasks fail

Ask: what capability is missing, and how do we make it legible and enforceable?

Fix the harness (docs, tests, scripts) — not just the immediate code.

## Repository conventions

- Update [CHANGELOG.md](../../CHANGELOG.md) for user-visible or harness changes
- Active work lives in `docs/exec-plans/active/`
- Architecture rules: [ARCHITECTURE.md](../../ARCHITECTURE.md)
- Golden principles: [docs/design-docs/golden-principles.md](../../docs/design-docs/golden-principles.md)

## Do not

- Hardcode credentials or secrets in source
- Add unrelated dependencies without security review
- Skip tests to force green CI
- Create monolithic AGENTS.md (>150 lines) — link to docs/ instead
